_refine_special_details
;
 Refinement of F^2^ against ALL reflections.  The weighted R-factor wR and 
 goodness of fit S are based on F^2^, conventional R-factors R are based 
 on F, with F set to zero for negative F^2^. The threshold expression of 
 F^2^ > 2sigma(F^2^) is used only for calculating R-factors(gt) etc. and is 
 not relevant to the choice of reflections for refinement.  R-factors based 
 on F^2^ are statistically about twice as large as those based on F, and R- 
 factors based on ALL data will be even larger. 
;
_olex2_refinement_description
;
1. Fixed Uiso
 At 1.2 times of:
  All C(H) groups, All C(H,H) groups
 At 1.5 times of:
  All N(H,H,H) groups
2. Restrained distances
 C3-Br1 \\sim C3A-Br1
 with sigma of 0.02
 C4-Br2 \\sim C4A-Br2
 with sigma of 0.02
3. Rigid bond restraints
 All non-hydrogen atoms
 with sigma for 1-2 distances of 0.01 and sigma for 1-3 distances of 0.01
4. Uiso/Uaniso restraints and constraints
All non-hydrogen atoms have similar U: within 1.7A with sigma of 0.04 and sigma
for terminal atoms of 0.08
5. Same fragment restrains
{N1, C1, C2, C3, C4}
as
{N1A, C1A, C2A, C3A, C4A}
6. Others
 Sof(Cl3B)=1-FVAR(1)
 Sof(Cl3A)=FVAR(1)
 Sof(N1A)=Sof(H1AA)=Sof(H1AB)=Sof(H1AC)=Sof(C1A)=Sof(H1AD)=Sof(H1AE)=Sof(C2A)=
 Sof(H2AA)=Sof(H2AB)=Sof(C3A)=Sof(H3A)=Sof(C4A)=Sof(H4AA)=Sof(H4AB)=1-FVAR(2)
 Sof(N1)=Sof(H1A)=Sof(H1B)=Sof(H1C)=Sof(C1)=Sof(H1D)=Sof(H1E)=Sof(C2)=Sof(H2A)=
 Sof(H2B)=Sof(C3)=Sof(H3)=Sof(C4)=Sof(H4A)=Sof(H4B)=FVAR(2)
 Fixed Sof: Cl1(0.5) Cl2(0.5)
7.a Ternary CH refined with riding coordinates:
 C3(H3), C3A(H3A)
7.b Secondary CH2 refined with riding coordinates:
 C1(H1D,H1E), C2(H2A,H2B), C4(H4A,H4B), C1A(H1AD,H1AE), C2A(H2AA,H2AB),
 C4A(H4AA,H4AB)
7.c Idealised Me refined as rotating group:
 N1(H1A,H1B,H1C), N1A(H1AA,H1AB,H1AC)
